# ── Contact form (EmailJS, client-side) ──────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the two values below. `.env` is
# gitignored.
#
# IMPORTANT: these VITE_* values are compiled into the public JS bundle —
# that's how EmailJS works in the browser, so they are NOT secret. Because
# anyone can read them, lock the account down in the EmailJS dashboard so the
# keys can't be used to spam through your account:
#   • Account → Security → set "Allowed origins" to your site
#     (https://dawnember.in, plus http://localhost:5173 for local dev).
#   • Enable reCAPTCHA on the email templates.
#   • Keep the built-in per-key rate limits on.
#
# The two templates and their recipients ("To email") are configured in the
# EmailJS dashboard; the template IDs live in src/mail.ts.

# EmailJS → Account → API Keys (the Public Key / User ID)
VITE_EMAILJS_PUBLIC_KEY=your_emailjs_public_key_here

# EmailJS → Email Services
VITE_EMAILJS_SERVICE_ID=your_emailjs_service_id_here
